---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Company"
  description="Why Honeypot R Us is building defensive deception, correlation, reversible quarantine, and owned playpens."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Yes, like Toys R Us</p>
      <h1>Security is serious. The wrong door can still be fun.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Honeypot R Us is a band of builders making defensive deception easier
        to deploy, safer to operate, and more useful after the first alert.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Catch early. Learn deeply. Respond proportionally.</h2>
        <p>
          A decoy touch is valuable because legitimate users had no reason to
          make it. The product around that signal determines whether the result
          is insight or another noisy alert.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="principles">
        <article class="principle">
          <h3>We sell safer uncertainty</h3>
          <p>
            Correlation raises or lowers confidence. It never turns a browser
            trait, IP address, or behavioral pattern into an identity claim.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <h3>We keep the mess on our side</h3>
          <p>
            A suspicious actor may enter an HNPT-owned isolated playpen. They
            are never dumped on an unrelated website or innocent third party.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <h3>We prefer typed evidence</h3>
          <p>
            Rust, Dart, and TypeScript lead the implementation; portable
            schemas and 17-language clients keep the perimeter broad.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle">
          <h3>We test the twin first</h3>
          <p>
            Repositories, migrations, packages, edge rules, and integrations
            prove themselves in the sibling test organization before promotion.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-muted">
    <div class="shell cta-band">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Open engineering</p>
        <h2>Follow the ecosystem as it grows.</h2>
        <p>
          Architecture, interfaces, clients, services, infrastructure, and test
          evidence live across the Honeypot R Us GitHub organization.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/honeypot-r-us">
          View GitHub
        </a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/developers/">Developers</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
